So the docs don't specify this anywhere that I could easily find it, but yes for some provider/model combinations it seems you have to specify the context limit in the provider block:
```json
"qwen/qwen3.6-35b-a3b": {
    "name": "Qwen3.6 35B a3b (local)",
    "options": {
        ...
    },
    "limit": {
        "context": 171352,
        "output": 20000
    }
}
```
this has me patched up. I could have swore that I didn't declare this with another local model, but maybe I'm mistaken. thanks all and hopefully this works for you as well @void0x14 !
